# PREVENTION AND MITIGATION OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN

REGENT OF REJANG LEBONG

BENGKULU PROVINCE

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF REJANG LEBONG REGENCY

NUMBER 4 OF 2015

CONCERNING

PREVENTION AND MITIGATION OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF REJANG LEBONG,

Considering:







a. that in order to guarantee the rights of women and children to participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and worth, and to receive protection from violence, discrimination and other violations of the rights of women and children, it is necessary to undertake prevention and mitigation efforts against violence toward women and children.
b. that in order for the prevention and mitigation efforts against violence toward women and children to obtain optimal results, and to be implemented quickly, in a planned, integrated, comprehensive and organized manner by involving all relevant elements in the region, it is necessary to regulate the prevention and mitigation of violence against women and child victims of violence.
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Prevention and Mitigation of Violence Against Women and Children.

In View of:







1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 28 of 1959 concerning Stipulation of Emergency Law Number 4 of 1956 (State Gazette of 1956 Number 55), Emergency Law Number 5 of 1956 (State Gazette of 1956 Number 56) And Emergency Law Number 6 of 1956 (State Gazette of 1956 Number 57) concerning Establishment of Level II Regions Including Municipalities, Within the Level I Region of South Sumatra, As Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1821);
